---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from "../site";

const UPDATED = "13 November 2026";
---

<Site title="Privacy policy" description="What personal data the SecureOne website and software collect: no cookies, analytics or telemetry. Your rights under India's DPDP Act.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" lead={`How SecureOne handles personal data on this website and in the software. Last updated ${UPDATED}.`} />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose reveal">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website and the SecureOne software are provided by SecureOne, India. In this policy, "we" and "us" mean
        SecureOne. For the personal data described here, we are the Data Fiduciary under India's Digital Personal Data
        Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act).
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>This website has no accounts, forms, cookies, analytics, advertising or tracking.</li>
        <li>The SecureOne software runs on your infrastructure. It sends no usage data, telemetry or user data to us.</li>
        <li>If you email us, we use what you send only to answer you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <h3>What our hosting provider records</h3>
      <p>
        The website is hosted by Vercel. Like any web server, it records technical data for each request: your IP
        address, browser type, the page requested and the time. This is used only to deliver the website and protect it
        from abuse, and is kept for a short period under Vercel's own policy. We do not combine it with other data or
        use it to identify you.
      </p>
      <h3>What stays in your browser</h3>
      <p>
        If you choose a light or dark theme, the choice is saved in your browser's local storage and is never sent to
        us. Documentation search runs entirely in your browser.
      </p>
      <h3>Links to other services</h3>
      <p>
        Links to Docker Hub, Render and other services take you to sites with their own privacy policies. Pulling the
        SecureOne image is handled by Docker Hub, not by us.
      </p>

      <h2>When you contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us, we receive your email address, your name if you include it, and your message. We use them only
        to answer you and follow up on your request, on the basis of your consent, which you give by writing to us. We
        delete them within 24 months of our last exchange, unless the law requires us to keep them longer. We do not
        sell or share them, and we do not use them for marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>The SecureOne software</h2>
      <p>
        SecureOne is self-hosted: you run it on infrastructure you choose, and it stores its data, including your users'
        accounts, in your own database. We have no access to it, and the software sends no usage data or telemetry to
        us.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the personal data of your users, you (the organisation running SecureOne) are the Data Fiduciary, and we are
        not involved in processing it. Features you turn on that connect to other services send data directly from your
        installation to those services, for example your email or SMS provider, CAPTCHA, social sign-in, log streaming
        and webhooks. The leaked-password check sends only the first five characters of a password's hash to Have I Been
        Pwned, never the password.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the DPDP Act you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what personal data of yours we hold and how we use it;</li>
        <li>correct, complete or update it;</li>
        <li>erase it, and withdraw any consent you gave;</li>
        <li>nominate someone to exercise these rights for you if you die or become unable to.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise these rights or raise a grievance, contact us (see below). We will reply within 30 days. If you are
        not satisfied with our answer, you can complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
      </p>

      <h2>Where data is processed</h2>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider may process the technical data described above on servers outside India, as the DPDP Act
        allows.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This website is meant for organisations and IT professionals, not for children, and we do not knowingly collect children's data.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we will publish the new version here with a new date.</p>

      <h2>Contact and grievances</h2>
      {SUPPORT_EMAIL ? (
        <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> with "Privacy" in the subject.</p>
      ) : (
        <p>Use the contact details on the <a href="/support/">Support</a> page, with "Privacy" in the subject.</p>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
